      "media": [],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "⚡️🇾🇪🇸🇦 Yemen Summary. October 5th.\n• Ansarallah captured the house of Saudi-backed “president” of Yemen, Rashad Al-Alimi. He recently announced the start of an offensive called “Dawn of Yemen” with the stated goal of retaking Sanaa. The offensive began with a large round of air strikes.\n• After another missile attack; the vital Saudi East-West pipeline is closed again.\n• The PLC began a counteroffensive attack in the Marib area, achieving some initial gains.\n• With the capture of Sha’ubah, Al-Ayn, and Al-A’loum, the Ansarallah encirclement of Ta’izz is now complete. \n• The PLC and Ansarallah have exchanged control of Murad and Dhubab airport, both located at the narrowest section of the Bab Al-Mandab Strait, a chokepoint for international shipping.\n• Yemeni ballistic missiles struck a Saudi ARAMCO refinery in Jeddah.\n• In an ugly turn of events, the PLC are uploading videos of themselves running over surrendering Ansarallah fighters with their vehicles.\n\n@MedmanNews",
